1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:06,910
Thanksgiving is in six days. I have a potluck sign-up sheet with forty-two names and zero desserts.

2
00:00:07,260 --> 00:00:12,416
Put me down for a pie. I'll bring the one from last year. It's aged.

3
00:00:12,766 --> 00:00:15,648
Chat wants to know if the pie is still legally food.

4
00:00:20,355 --> 00:00:23,739
Family! Our lives are about to change forever!

5
00:00:24,089 --> 00:00:28,875
You said that about the hot tub. We still don't have water in it. We have Earl in it.

6
00:00:29,225 --> 00:00:36,591
Bulk Galaxy. Black Friday. Doorbuster. An eighty-five inch TV. For forty-nine dollars.

7
00:00:37,941 --> 00:00:43,712
There are only three in stock. And I'm going to camp outside the store until the doors open.

8
00:00:44,062 --> 00:00:47,525
Dale, the doors open Friday! That's six days!

9
00:00:47,875 --> 00:00:55,120
Six days of camping for a TV that will last a lifetime. Or eighteen months. Whichever comes first.

10
00:00:56,470 --> 00:01:01,836
Back in sixty-two, I camped out for a TV. Four days in the snow.

11
00:01:02,386 --> 00:01:06,399
It only got one channel. The weather in Canada.

12
00:01:06,749 --> 00:01:15,791
I watched it for nine years. To this day, I know exactly when it's going to rain in Winnipeg. I'm never wrong. Nobody asks.

13
00:01:17,541 --> 00:01:21,849
Chat's starting a pool on what breaks first. Dad's back, Dad's spirit, or the tent.

14
00:01:22,199 --> 00:01:27,281
Nothing breaks! I bought a sleeping bag rated for minus forty degrees!

15
00:01:27,631 --> 00:01:28,764
With what money?

16
00:01:30,114 --> 00:01:35,151
With the TV money. So now I need the TV to be really, really cheap.

17
00:01:38,701 --> 00:01:44,451
People of Lower Fairview. In these tough economic times, your mayor has made a tough decision.

18
00:01:44,801 --> 00:01:47,288
I have sold the naming rights to Thanksgiving.

19
00:01:48,638 --> 00:01:49,958
You can do that?

20
00:01:50,308 --> 00:01:53,948
Nobody said I couldn't. That's the whole secret of government.

21
00:01:54,298 --> 00:01:59,667
From now on, it is officially "Bulk Galaxy Thanks-Buying, Presented by Bulk Galaxy."

22
00:02:01,017 --> 00:02:02,737
Do I still get turkey?

23
00:02:03,087 --> 00:02:06,599
You get a coupon for ten percent off a turkey-shaped candle.

24
00:02:11,164 --> 00:02:16,609
Doreen! The HOA potluck is on Thursday. It's been on Thursday for nineteen years!

25
00:02:17,959 --> 00:02:26,113
Not anymore, Tammy. Bulk Galaxy needs Thursday for "early access." Thanksgiving is now Wednesday. From four to four-fifteen.

26
00:02:26,463 --> 00:02:30,163
Fifteen minutes?! You can't even thaw a turkey in fifteen minutes!

27
00:02:30,513 --> 00:02:35,848
Bulk Galaxy sells pre-thawed turkeys. Pre-chewed, too. It's very convenient.

28
00:02:37,198 --> 00:02:41,947
This means war, Doreen. HOA war. The worst kind. With bylaws.

29
00:02:42,297 --> 00:02:46,193
Bring it, Tammy. I have a corporate sponsor. What do you have?

30
00:02:46,543 --> 00:02:48,845
Forty-two casseroles and a grudge.

31
00:02:51,862 --> 00:02:53,631
Mayor, should I be worried?

32
00:02:53,981 --> 00:02:59,968
Officer, you're in charge of crowd control on Friday. Bulk Galaxy is paying you in gift cards.

33
00:03:00,318 --> 00:03:05,159
I've never controlled a crowd. I once controlled a duck. For a minute.

34
00:03:06,709 --> 00:03:11,279
Day one. Number one in line. History will remember this tent.

35
00:03:11,629 --> 00:03:18,889
Sleeping bag. Camping stove. Six cans of beans. And a bucket for... after the beans.

36
00:03:22,453 --> 00:03:26,233
Morning, Dale. I see you're number two in line.

37
00:03:27,583 --> 00:03:30,394
Number two? I'm the only one here!

38
00:03:30,744 --> 00:03:37,057
My lawn chair has been here since Tuesday. Holding my place. That's a legal placeholder.

39
00:03:37,407 --> 00:03:41,185
That's not a chair, Gary! That's a stick with a napkin on it!

40
00:03:42,535 --> 00:03:49,081
It's a minimalist chair. You wouldn't understand. You buy furniture with the word "Bonanza" in it.

41
00:03:49,431 --> 00:03:52,568
Fine. Then I'm putting up a bigger tent.

42
00:03:52,918 --> 00:03:59,047
My brother-in-law is bringing an R.V. With a hot tub. With water in it, Dale.

43
00:04:00,397 --> 00:04:04,550
He knows about the hot tub. Everybody knows about the hot tub.

44
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:09,348
Okay, we're live. Welcome to "Planet Line." A nature documentary.

45
00:04:09,698 --> 00:04:15,539
I'm the narrator. I've been practicing my British voice. Listen. Hello.

46
00:04:16,889 --> 00:04:18,433
That was your normal voice.

47
00:04:18,783 --> 00:04:19,981
Thank you.

48
00:04:20,331 --> 00:04:28,001
Today we observe the North American Doorbuster. A rare creature that migrates to a parking lot once a year to fight over electronics.

49
00:04:29,351 --> 00:04:33,620
Look! The male is building his nest out of a sleeping bag and shame.

50
00:04:33,970 --> 00:04:36,925
That's my dad. Chat has named him "The Bean Elk."

51
00:04:37,275 --> 00:04:41,403
Somebody donated twenty bucks to see the Bean Elk fight the Pink Polo.

52
00:04:42,753 --> 00:04:46,683
Nature is brutal, Jace. We don't interfere. We monetize.

53
00:04:47,233 --> 00:04:51,323
Listen up. The Mayor moved Thanksgiving. So we are moving the Mayor.

54
00:04:51,673 --> 00:04:56,907
Operation Gravy Boat. Forty-two households. Every casserole has a code name.

55
00:04:58,257 --> 00:05:00,015
What's my code name?

56
00:05:00,365 --> 00:05:01,522
"Liability."

57
00:05:01,872 --> 00:05:07,054
I've been called worse. In Korea they called me "Sir, Please Put That Down."

58
00:05:08,404 --> 00:05:15,754
Tammy, I have analyzed your battle plan. Your weakest unit is the green bean casserole. Nobody wants it.

59
00:05:16,104 --> 00:05:22,130
The green bean casserole is a tradition. Nobody wants traditions. That's how you know they're traditions.

60
00:05:22,480 --> 00:05:28,801
Also, Dale has called me eleven times from the parking lot to ask if beans can expire inside a person.

61
00:05:30,151 --> 00:05:35,192
Good. Let him suffer. Earl, you're on surveillance. Watch the Mayor's office.

62
00:05:35,542 --> 00:05:41,318
Surveillance. Back in seventy-five, I spied on a whole town for the government.

63
00:05:41,868 --> 00:05:48,339
I sat in this diner for six years with a newspaper. I had holes cut in it for my eyes.

64
00:05:48,689 --> 00:05:56,622
Nobody ever told me what I was looking for. I just ordered a lot of soup. The government still owes me for soup.

65
00:05:58,372 --> 00:06:01,357
Just watch the office, Earl. And bring your own soup.

66
00:06:01,907 --> 00:06:08,322
All right, people. Day three. I'm crowd control. Everybody stay calm and form a line.

67
00:06:09,672 --> 00:06:13,334
We are the line, Officer. We've been the line since Saturday.

68
00:06:13,684 --> 00:06:18,434
Then form a better one. Straighter. With more... feeling.

69
00:06:18,784 --> 00:06:24,260
Officer, behind me there are now two hundred people. You know what that makes my spot?

70
00:06:25,610 --> 00:06:26,681
Crowded?

71
00:06:27,031 --> 00:06:33,331
Valuable! I am selling shares in my spot. Ten dollars buys you one percent of standing here.

72
00:06:33,681 --> 00:06:39,714
Amateur. I'm selling line futures. You pay me now for a spot I might have next year.

73
00:06:41,064 --> 00:06:47,865
Then I'm selling line insurance! If Gary's spot doesn't exist, I pay you nothing! That's the policy!

74
00:06:48,215 --> 00:06:49,499
I'll take two.

75
00:06:49,849 --> 00:06:55,667
My R.V. just arrived, Dale. It has a hot tub and a chocolate fountain.

76
00:06:57,017 --> 00:07:04,479
Oh yeah? I just rented my sleeping bag to a man for two hours. He cried in it. I charged extra.

77
00:07:04,829 --> 00:07:06,821
You're monetizing grief?

78
00:07:07,171 --> 00:07:14,355
It's called the line economy, Gary. Everything here is for sale. Except the bucket. The bucket is personal.

79
00:07:15,705 --> 00:07:19,591
Dale, a lady at the back is offering three hundred bucks for your spot.

80
00:07:19,941 --> 00:07:23,149
Three hundred?! The TV is forty-nine!

81
00:07:24,299 --> 00:07:30,644
No. It's not about the money. It's about the TV. I'm holding. Diamond hands.

82
00:07:31,994 --> 00:07:37,811
I'll take her three hundred. And then I'll get back in line. Behind my chair.

83
00:07:38,161 --> 00:07:39,497
Is that legal?

84
00:07:39,847 --> 00:07:42,506
You tell me. You're the law.

85
00:07:43,856 --> 00:07:46,401
I really wish people would stop telling me that.

86
00:07:46,951 --> 00:07:54,425
Day four on Planet Line. The herd has grown to six hundred. There's a guy selling hot dogs from inside his coat.

87
00:07:54,775 --> 00:07:58,767
Don't buy one. That's not a hot dog. That's just his arm in a bun.

88
00:08:00,117 --> 00:08:08,047
Oh no. Two males are fighting over the last outlet. One is plugging in a phone. The other is plugging in a mini fridge.

89
00:08:08,397 --> 00:08:14,160
The mini fridge always wins. It has nothing to lose. It's already cold inside. Like my dad.

90
00:08:14,510 --> 00:08:20,501
Kyle! A nature channel wants to buy the stream. They want to know if your dad is endangered.

91
00:08:21,851 --> 00:08:24,915
Tell them he's not endangered. He's just not doing well.

92
00:08:25,465 --> 00:08:32,260
Doreen. My potluck has been rescheduled. Thursday. At four a.m. In front of Bulk Galaxy.

93
00:08:32,610 --> 00:08:34,737
You're bringing Thanksgiving to the line?!

94
00:08:36,087 --> 00:08:44,165
If the town won't come to the potluck, the potluck comes to the town. With folding tables. And a permit I laminated an hour ago.

95
00:08:44,515 --> 00:08:49,837
That's unlicensed gravy! Bulk Galaxy has exclusive gravy rights in this town!

96
00:08:50,187 --> 00:08:51,614
You sold the GRAVY?

97
00:08:52,964 --> 00:08:59,647
I sold the gravy, the stuffing, and the concept of being grateful. Gratitude now costs four ninety-nine a month.

98
00:08:59,997 --> 00:09:02,163
Doreen, what else did you sell?

99
00:09:02,513 --> 00:09:09,354
The park. The library. The word "Wednesday." If you say it on the radio, Bulk Galaxy gets a nickel.

100
00:09:10,704 --> 00:09:16,260
Also your street. It's called "Doorbuster Lane" now. You live at four-twelve Doorbuster Lane.

101
00:09:16,610 --> 00:09:21,550
Then I'll see you on Doorbuster Lane, Doreen. Bring your appetite. And a helmet.

102
00:09:23,924 --> 00:09:29,288
She thinks she can fight capitalism with casseroles. Adorable. I'll sell that too.

103
00:09:29,838 --> 00:09:35,760
Brought you a thermos, son. It's soup. Government soup. They finally paid me.

104
00:09:36,110 --> 00:09:41,244
Thanks, Earl. Day five. I can't feel my legs. I sold them.

105
00:09:41,594 --> 00:09:43,350
You sold your legs?!

106
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:50,423
The feeling in them. A guy bought my numbness for twenty bucks. It's the line economy.

107
00:09:50,773 --> 00:09:57,864
Earl! Come over to the R.V. I've got a hot tub, a chocolate fountain, and a man who plays the harp.

108
00:09:58,214 --> 00:10:00,057
Is it a real harp?

109
00:10:01,407 --> 00:10:04,986
It's a cheese slicer. But he really commits.

110
00:10:05,336 --> 00:10:09,906
This line reminds me of the great bread line of sixty-seven.

111
00:10:10,456 --> 00:10:16,349
There was no bread. Just a line. People heard there was a line, so they got in it.

112
00:10:16,699 --> 00:10:25,254
Lasted eleven years. Two weddings. One war. At the front, there was just a guy. He was also waiting.

113
00:10:27,004 --> 00:10:29,600
Earl, what happened to the guy at the front?

114
00:10:29,950 --> 00:10:32,753
He's still there. I bring him soup.

115
00:10:34,103 --> 00:10:40,366
Good night, Dale. My R.V. has a heated toilet. It sings to me.

116
00:10:40,716 --> 00:10:46,167
Enjoy it, Gary. Tomorrow I get the TV. And you get a stick with a napkin on it.

117
00:10:46,717 --> 00:10:53,230
Four a.m. Operation Gravy Boat is live. Tables, deploy! Casseroles, flank left!

118
00:10:54,580 --> 00:11:00,189
Officer! Arrest that woman! She's handing out free stuffing! In front of a store!

119
00:11:00,539 --> 00:11:02,484
Is free stuffing a crime?

120
00:11:02,834 --> 00:11:07,370
It is now. I sold the free. Free is a Bulk Galaxy trademark.

121
00:11:08,720 --> 00:11:15,330
Then it's not free. It's a doorbuster. Zero dollars. Limit one per customer. While supplies last.

122
00:11:15,680 --> 00:11:19,339
Ooh. Limited supply. Now I want it more.

123
00:11:19,689 --> 00:11:25,866
The line is leaving! They're going to the potluck! They're eating sweet potatoes! With marshmallows!

124
00:11:27,216 --> 00:11:31,967
That's the HOA, Doreen. We don't have money. But we have mini marshmallows.

125
00:11:32,317 --> 00:11:36,854
Fine! Officer, tell the store to open the doors early! Now!

126
00:11:37,204 --> 00:11:41,579
I don't have a radio. I have a whistle. And it's full of gravy.

127
00:11:42,929 --> 00:11:45,782
Wait. Doreen, what did you just do?

128
00:11:46,132 --> 00:11:52,355
I made an announcement. Bulk Galaxy is opening in sixty seconds. And there are only three TVs.

129
00:11:52,905 --> 00:11:56,903
Okay! Everybody stay calm! Walk, don't run!

130
00:11:58,253 --> 00:12:02,568
They're running! Why is everyone running?! I said the opposite!

131
00:12:02,918 --> 00:12:08,591
Chat, we are witnessing the great migration. Six hundred people. One door. Zero dignity.

132
00:12:08,941 --> 00:12:13,533
I'm number one! I have six days of beans in me! Out of my way!

133
00:12:16,788 --> 00:12:20,948
My chair was here first! My chair was here first!

134
00:12:22,964 --> 00:12:28,288
Somebody just took my hat! And my belt! They're selling my belt in aisle four!

135
00:12:28,638 --> 00:12:32,807
A grandma just suplexed a man for a waffle iron. Nature is healing.

136
00:12:34,157 --> 00:12:38,452
Is this... is this crowd control? Am I doing it?

137
00:12:38,802 --> 00:12:42,758
You're doing it, Officer. The crowd is controlling you. That counts.

138
00:12:43,308 --> 00:12:46,905
There it is! The last box! It's mine!

139
00:12:48,255 --> 00:12:51,488
It's mine! I paid my chair rent!

140
00:12:54,862 --> 00:13:00,862
Folks, the two alpha males are circling the final box. In the wild, this is where one of them pees on it.

141
00:13:01,212 --> 00:13:02,764
Don't you dare, Gary.

142
00:13:04,114 --> 00:13:09,203
I had six days of chocolate fountain, Dale. I'm not the one you should worry about.

143
00:13:09,553 --> 00:13:14,777
I sold my legs for this! I rented out my sorrow! Give me that TV!

144
00:13:15,127 --> 00:13:18,931
He jumped! He jumped over the cheese slicer guy!

145
00:13:20,281 --> 00:13:26,726
Got it! The eighty-five inch TV! It's mine! It's... surprisingly light.

146
00:13:27,076 --> 00:13:29,598
The box is the size of a sandwich.

147
00:13:30,148 --> 00:13:36,534
Family. Six days. Two hundred cans of beans. One TV. Behold.

148
00:13:37,884 --> 00:13:39,947
That's an eight point five inch TV.

149
00:13:40,297 --> 00:13:41,734
Eight POINT five?!

150
00:13:42,084 --> 00:13:46,669
There's a decimal on the flyer, Dale. It's very small. Like the TV.

151
00:13:48,019 --> 00:13:49,764
I thought that was a crumb.

152
00:13:50,114 --> 00:13:53,073
Turn it on. Let's see what it gets.

153
00:13:53,423 --> 00:13:57,329
It only gets one channel. It's an ad for next year's Black Friday.

154
00:13:58,679 --> 00:14:01,802
The weather in Canada! It's back!

155
00:14:02,152 --> 00:14:03,761
No, Grandpa, it's an ad.

156
00:14:04,111 --> 00:14:10,536
It's going to rain in Winnipeg Tuesday. Nobody asked. Nobody ever asks.

157
00:14:11,886 --> 00:14:17,529
Meanwhile, my potluck fed six hundred people. And Doreen. Doreen had four plates.

158
00:14:17,879 --> 00:14:19,436
What happened to Gary?

159
00:14:19,786 --> 00:14:25,822
Gary sold his R.V. to buy line futures. For next year. He's living in the lawn chair now.

160
00:14:27,172 --> 00:14:32,535
Wait. The nature channel bought Planet Line. Jace and I got paid. Four hundred dollars.

161
00:14:32,885 --> 00:14:36,501
Four hundred dollars! Kyle, that's eight TVs!

162
00:14:36,851 --> 00:14:40,721
That's eight tiny TVs, Dad. Stacked, they make one normal TV.

163
00:14:42,271 --> 00:14:46,129
Homi. Do you think I wasted six days of my life?

164
00:14:46,479 --> 00:14:52,874
No, Dale. You also wasted forty-nine dollars, your legs, and a bucket I will not discuss.

165
00:14:53,424 --> 00:14:59,964
Great news, Lower Fairview. Black Friday was a record. Bulk Galaxy is so happy, they bought Christmas.

166
00:15:01,314 --> 00:15:03,164
What's Christmas called now?

167
00:15:03,514 --> 00:15:08,179
"Christmas." But every time you say it, a little bell rings, and you owe a dollar.

168
00:15:08,529 --> 00:15:11,809
I just said it in my head. Do I owe a dollar?

169
00:15:13,159 --> 00:15:15,448
Two. Thinking is premium.

170
00:15:15,798 --> 00:15:17,996
You know, I learned something today.

171
00:15:18,346 --> 00:15:22,583
The holidays aren't about the stuff. They're about getting there first.

172
00:15:23,933 --> 00:15:27,047
That's why next year I'm camping out in July.

173
00:15:27,397 --> 00:15:32,356
That's beautiful, Dale. I'm gonna camp behind you. For crowd control.

174
00:15:32,706 --> 00:15:38,165
Excellent. The spot in front of Dale is available. Starting bid: Dale's house.

